      <activity id="e2473193-1c79-51a7-bd4b-9e81503f6b51" activityNameId="e7436754-59be-58fa-b914-e730cea04e19" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, at cogen 50kWth, biomethane, economic allocation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, at cogen 50kWth, biomethane, economic allocation
Inventory for 1 MJ heat from biomethane, burned in a cogeneration unit with a capacity of 50 kWth. The multioutput process "biomethane, burned in cogen 50kWth delivers the coproducts "heat, at cogen 50kWth, biomethane, allocation exergy" and "electricity, at cogen 50kWth, biomethane, allocation exergy". The energy efficiency is 29% for electricity and 62% for heat. The economic factor is 0.72 for electricity and 0.28 for heat. This leads to the allocation factor of 0.55 for electricity and 0.45 for heat.;
Synonyms: Strom, ab BHKW 50kWth, Biogas, aufbereitet, ökonomische Allokation; 
UUID: 51a3bcc8-538c-30a6-a103-1ff9eba008d8
Included are the biomethane burning in a 50 kWth cogen unit which in turn includes fuel input, infrastructure (boiler), air and water emissions and electrictiy needed for operation. The efficiency and economic allocation is considered
Location: Data apply to the combustion in Switzerland.
Technology: efficiency of average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_51a3bcc8-538c-30a6-a103-1ff9eba008d8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
